  "reasoning": "The claim that humans use only 10% of their brains is a well-known, widely debunked neurological myth. Brain imaging technologies such as fMRI and PET scans demonstrate that virtually all parts of the brain are active and have specific functions, even during simple tasks or sleep. Furthermore, evolutionary biology and clinical neurology show that unused brain areas would degenerate or atrophy over time; even minor damage to small regions of the brain often results in noticeable cognitive, sensory, or motor deficits. Neuroscientists widely agree that there is no large, dormant 90% portion of the brain waiting to be unlocked.",
